From: DroidVM bring-up <build@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] owner cache: say why the SystemOS mount was refused

The owner chain is silent on failure: native_owner_cache_prepare() returns an
errno, the caller goes on to exec init against whatever root it has, and the only
symptom the guest shows is dyld's "no dyld cache" -- libSystem lives in the
SystemOS volume, which is the thing that was not mounted.

With the boot argument owner-cache-diag=1, turn that errno into a panic.  The
panic log is the one channel this board can be read through (this kernel has no
serial console), and it carries everything needed to tell the stages apart:

  stage 0  the OS root itself was not authorized (trust roots, or the check)
  stage 1  the SystemOS volume was never published by the block driver (10 s wait)
  stage 2  the mount payload could not be copied out
  stage 3  mount() failed -- mount_status holds its errno
  stage 4  mounted, but not authorized or not a native union at "/"
  stage 5+ the environment hand-off failed

dev/selected are the dev_t the root is on and the one the SystemOS volume
resolved to; path is what the block driver named it.  autherr/decision come from
the root-authorization audit in bsd_init.

The check is behind a boot argument so an ordinary build of this patch is inert.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -186,6 +186,31 @@
 			native_owner_cache_dyld_flags = dyld_flags;
 		}
 	#endif
 		native_owner_cache_authorized = cache_authorized;
+		/*
+		 * DroidVM: report the refusal instead of leaving the guest to fail later
+		 * with dyld's "no dyld cache".  Gated on owner-cache-diag=1 so an ordinary
+		 * build of this patch boots exactly as before.
+		 */
+		if (error) {
+			extern volatile int native_owner_root_apple_autherr;
+			extern volatile int native_owner_root_decision;
+			extern int PE_parse_boot_argn(const char *, void *, int);
+			int diag = 0;
+
+			if (PE_parse_boot_argn("owner-cache-diag", &diag, sizeof(diag)) && diag) {
+				panic("DroidVM owner-cache: stage=%d status=%d mount=%d root_auth=%d "
+				    "autherr=%d decision=%d dev=%d/%d path=%s",
+				    native_owner_cache_stage, error,
+				    native_owner_cache_mount_status, root_authorized,
+				    native_owner_root_apple_autherr, native_owner_root_decision,
+				    (int)root_device, (int)selected,
+				    native_owner_cache_device_path);
+			}
+		}
 		native_owner_cache_status = error;
 		native_owner_cache_checkpoint(error, cache_authorized);
 		return error;
 	}
 #endif
